<Layout title="Privacy | Trustora" description="Trustora's plain-language privacy notice." currentPath="/legal/privacy/">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="measure page-hero-grid"><div class="page-hero-copy"><SectionLabel>Legal / Privacy</SectionLabel><h1>A clear note on privacy.</h1><p>Last updated: August 11, 2026. This site is intentionally simple and does not use analytics, advertising, or chat scripts.</p></div><div class="page-hero-note">If you contact Trustora, your message is used to respond to your inquiry and handled by the people responsible for that conversation.</div></div></section>
  <section class="section cream-field"><div class="measure legal-layout"><aside><SectionLabel>Privacy notice</SectionLabel></aside><div class="prose"><h2>What this site collects</h2><p>Trustora does not intentionally collect personal information merely because you browse this website. The site does not use advertising cookies, analytics scripts, or third-party chat tools.</p><h2>When you contact us</h2><p>If you choose to email Trustora or submit a form, you may provide your name, work email, company, country, role, and the context you choose to share. We use that information to respond to your request and decide whether a conversation is appropriate.</p><h2>What not to send</h2><p>Please do not send passport details, payroll records, government identifiers, health information, or other sensitive personal information through this website.</p><h2>Questions</h2><p>For privacy questions, email <a href="mailto:info@trustora.net">info@trustora.net</a>.</p></div></div></section>
</Layout>
